 "description": "A second continuation, each statistic's target set from its own noise (description; discarded seeds).\n\nThe first continuation (`hinge.py`) passed the wild type in 2 of 5 populations with every mutant in\n5 of 5, its failures statistics parked just inside their bars. Graded on 15 populations\n(`noise_measure.json`) its answer passes the wild type in 8; the spread between populations is\nsmall for most statistics and large for pre-exit enrichment (SD 1.17 in z), whose exits are few.\n\nFrom that answer, with the first continuation's search state carried over (its sigma and\nper-parameter steps at its end), sep-CMA on the same objective: stage 3's (the six families plus\ntph-1's, pdfr-1's and tax-4's lawn differences, the mutants half of it, both guards) plus a hinge,\n5 x the sum over statistics of max(0, |10\u00b7asinh(z/10)| - target)^2, each statistic's target its\npass rule's bar (3.0781 for a wild-type statistic, 2.24 for a mutant's) less 1.65 x its SD between\nthe 15 populations, so a statistic held at its target passes a population 95% of the time.\n50 generations, population 48 at 200 animals on 16 workers, readouts every 10 generations with\nevery statistic recorded. The verdict as stage 3's: the last answer graded with presence on 5 fresh\npopulations passes the wild type in at least 3 and tph-1 and tax-4 each in at least 3.\n\nSeeds: candidates 864,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i, CMA 9501, readouts 865,000,000 + i, the grade\n866,000,000 + 200\u00b7g + i. Run from the repository root.\n",
